course: dictionary
lesson: 2785
title: Dishwasher: a machine or a person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dishwasher is a machine in the kitchen that washes plates, cups, cutlery and pans with hot water and soap. The word can also mean a person whose job is washing dishes, for example in a restaurant. When a word has two meanings, read the sentence to see which one fits.
explain: «Helping with the washing up or loading the dishwasher is useful work at home.» Here you load something, so dishwasher means the machine. Ask yourself: does this sentence describe a thing or a person? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Context also gives safety clues. «Wait a few minutes and stand back when opening a dishwasher that has just finished, because hot steam can scald.» The words wait, stand back and scald tell you the machine can be hot and dangerous. The sentence does not say the machine is broken, so do not add that idea.
fact: A dishwasher is a machine that cleans dirty dishes with hot water and soap.
fact: A dishwasher can also be a person whose job is washing dishes, such as in a restaurant.
fact: Dishwasher tablets and liquid are dangerous to swallow, so keep them away from small children.
fact: Do not open a dishwasher during its cycle, and wait a few minutes after it finishes, because hot steam can scald.
fact: Washing-up liquid must never go in a dishwasher, because its foam would overflow.
exercise: «Helping with the washing up or loading the dishwasher is useful work at home.» What is a dishwasher in this sentence? | A tidy kitchen floor | A person who lives at home | A cupboard under the kitchen sink | *A machine that washes dishes with hot water and soap
exercise: Which sentence uses dishwasher to mean a person? | Mum put the dishwasher on before bed. | The dishwasher was switched on after tea. | *The restaurant's dishwasher washed all the pans after dinner. | The dishwasher tablets were kept under the sink.
exercise: «Wait a few minutes and stand back when opening a dishwasher that has just finished, because hot steam can scald.» Find and copy one word that warns you to be careful. | dishwasher | *scald | minutes | kitchen
test: «Open the cupboard under the kitchen sink and you will find dishwasher tablets.» What does the list of strong chemicals tell you about dishwasher tablets? | *They are dangerous, so keep them away from small children | They are a kind of dessert | They clean the floor | They are sweets for a treat
test: Why must you stand back when opening a dishwasher that has just finished? | To check for a lost sock | To stop the plates from falling out | *Because hot steam can scald you | Because it is very quiet
exam: Nadia says, «The dishwasher at the café is very busy tonight.» Which meaning fits best? | A tap for hot water | A machine in the kitchen that washes plates | *A person whose job is washing dishes | A kind of washing-up liquid
